WEBVTT

00:00:02.002 --> 00:00:03.970
Good health, strong body,
clear mind.

00:00:04.037 --> 00:00:06.301
And you.
Your hospitality

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:09.172
your generosity, your patience.

00:00:09.209 --> 00:00:10.699
Many thanks.

00:00:10.744 --> 00:00:13.474
My colleague's behavior...

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:15.640
our apologies.

00:00:15.682 --> 00:00:17.673
Consul, I assure you,
I intended...

00:00:17.717 --> 00:00:19.446
Please make her quiet.

00:00:19.486 --> 00:00:20.544
Captain, please.

00:00:20.587 --> 00:00:22.214
I understand.

00:00:22.255 --> 00:00:25.224
Good health, strong body,
clear mind.

00:00:26.626 --> 00:00:28.526
And you.

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:32.292
Your journey home
short and safe.

00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:43.104
Captain's Log, Stardate 50425.1.

00:00:43.143 --> 00:00:46.237
Mr. Neelix and I have completed
our three-day trade mission

00:00:46.279 --> 00:00:49.146
with the Tak Tak,
one of the more unusual species

00:00:49.182 --> 00:00:51.377
we've encountered
in the Delta Quadrant.

00:00:51.418 --> 00:00:53.648
We are en route back to Voyager.

00:00:55.588 --> 00:00:57.419
Oh...

00:00:57.457 --> 00:01:00.119
I've always been taught
to be tolerant

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:01.957
of other cultures
and points of view...

00:01:02.062 --> 00:01:03.689
no matter how alien...

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:05.197
but I have to say
that the Tak Tak

00:01:05.231 --> 00:01:07.699
are the most unforgiving people
I've ever met.

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:09.964
They are a little impatient.

00:01:10.036 --> 00:01:12.095
They make the Klingons
look sedate.

00:01:12.138 --> 00:01:14.606
I may never put my hands
on my hips again.

00:01:14.641 --> 00:01:16.233
You had no way of knowing

00:01:16.276 --> 00:01:19.837
you were making one
of the worst insults possible.

00:01:19.879 --> 00:01:22.404
Obviously, they've never heard
of "forgive and forget."

00:01:22.449 --> 00:01:23.973
It's a good thing
you were there, Mr. Neelix.

00:01:24.084 --> 00:01:25.984
I might have been shot at dawn.

00:01:26.052 --> 00:01:28.384
I have studied
chromolinguistics,

00:01:28.421 --> 00:01:29.979
American Sign Language,

00:01:30.056 --> 00:01:32.388
the gestural idioms
of the Leyron,

00:01:32.425 --> 00:01:35.326
but I just couldn't get the hang
of the Tak Tak.

00:01:35.361 --> 00:01:38.762
It seemed like more than just
a language to me, Captain.

00:01:38.798 --> 00:01:40.925
A lot of their gestures,

00:01:40.967 --> 00:01:43.435
from what I could tell,
were ritualistic...

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:44.994
you might even say
superstitious.

00:01:45.038 --> 00:01:48.997
You have a genuine flair
for diplomacy, Mr. Neelix.

00:01:49.075 --> 00:01:51.475
I may have to promote you...

00:01:51.511 --> 00:01:54.412
from morale officer
to ambassador.

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:56.347
With all the species
we're bound to meet,

00:01:56.382 --> 00:01:58.543
I could use a man like you
at the front door.

00:01:59.786 --> 00:02:01.879
Ambassador Neelix.

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:04.014
I like the sound of that.

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:08.251
We're approaching
the rendezvous coordinates.

00:02:08.294 --> 00:02:10.262
Dropping to one-quarter impulse.

00:02:12.632 --> 00:02:13.929
Voyager's not there.

00:02:13.967 --> 00:02:15.594
And they're not responding
to hails.

00:02:15.635 --> 00:02:19.162
I'm running a long-range scan.

00:02:19.205 --> 00:02:20.695
There they are.

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:22.901
They're holding position
in Sector 38.

00:02:22.942 --> 00:02:25.502
Coordinates 121 mark 6.

00:02:25.545 --> 00:02:27.979
That's over a light-year
away from here.

00:02:28.047 --> 00:02:29.947
The ship appears to be adrift.

00:02:29.983 --> 00:02:31.644
They could be in trouble.

00:02:31.684 --> 00:02:33.675
Engaging maximum warp.

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:42.455
Janeway to Voyager.

00:02:42.495 --> 00:02:44.793
Commander Chakotay, respond.

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:48.933
The ship looks perfectly fine.

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:50.993
There's no sign
of any external damage.

00:02:51.104 --> 00:02:52.469
Is there any sign of the crew?

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:55.099
There's some kind
of bioelectric interference.

00:02:55.141 --> 00:02:57.234
I can't get clear
life sign readings.

00:02:57.277 --> 00:02:59.768
The escape pods are all in place

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:01.871
and there's no indication
of any recent

00:03:01.915 --> 00:03:03.382
transporter activity.

00:03:03.416 --> 00:03:05.611
Grab a phaser, Ambassador.

00:03:05.652 --> 00:03:07.643
We're going to get some answers.

00:05:08.273 --> 00:05:10.503
Still no sign of the crew,

00:05:10.542 --> 00:05:13.136
but these sensor readings
are highly erratic.

00:05:13.178 --> 00:05:15.169
The bioelectric field
is permeating the ship.

00:05:15.213 --> 00:05:16.737
Where's it coming from?

00:05:16.782 --> 00:05:18.409
I can't localize it.

00:05:18.450 --> 00:05:21.351
Let's try accessing
the ship's internal sensors.

00:05:21.386 --> 00:05:24.253
See if we can get
a better reading.

00:05:33.298 --> 00:05:34.856
Same problem.

00:05:34.900 --> 00:05:36.891
The main computer's off-line.

00:05:36.935 --> 00:05:38.903
So is the com system.

00:05:38.937 --> 00:05:41.235
This is strange.

00:05:41.273 --> 00:05:44.436
One of the bio-neural gel packs
in the Mess Hall ruptured,

00:05:44.476 --> 00:05:48.776
but most of the systems in there
seem to be functioning normally.

00:05:48.814 --> 00:05:51.305
Let's get to the Bridge.

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:04.757
Someone was doing maintenance
work on this power relay.

00:06:04.796 --> 00:06:06.855
All the equipment
is still active,

00:06:06.898 --> 00:06:09.696
but the work hasn't
been completed.

00:06:09.735 --> 00:06:12.602
It's almost as if they dropped
what they were doing and ran.

00:06:13.605 --> 00:06:15.470
Come on.

00:06:19.111 --> 00:06:20.305
This certainly isn't

00:06:20.345 --> 00:06:22.336
the welcome home
I was expecting.

00:06:22.381 --> 00:06:25.316
Me neither, but if there was
an attack of some kind,

00:06:25.350 --> 00:06:27.284
why didn't Chakotay try
to contact us

00:06:27.319 --> 00:06:28.650
or send out a warning buoy?

00:06:29.821 --> 00:06:32.847
I'm picking up a com signal
about ten meters ahead.

00:06:36.828 --> 00:06:38.955
It's coming
from inside this room.

00:06:39.031 --> 00:06:41.226
This is Ensign Wildman's
quarters.

00:06:41.266 --> 00:06:43.461
Is she in there?

00:06:43.502 --> 00:06:44.969
I can't tell.

00:06:45.003 --> 00:06:46.561
Let's take a look.

00:06:46.605 --> 00:06:48.072
Stand ready.

00:06:50.475 --> 00:06:52.375
Coming up next,

00:06:52.411 --> 00:06:55.073
our very special guest,
Ensign Kaplan.

00:06:55.113 --> 00:06:57.308
She's going to be sharing her...

00:06:57.349 --> 00:06:58.839
Here's our com signal...

00:06:58.884 --> 00:07:00.852
your Good Morning, Voyager
program.

00:07:00.886 --> 00:07:04.287
Ensign Wildman is one
of my most dedicated viewers.

00:07:04.322 --> 00:07:07.155
According to the time index,

00:07:07.192 --> 00:07:10.889
she activated this program
approximately 11 hours ago.

00:07:10.929 --> 00:07:12.089
Why is it still running?

00:07:12.130 --> 00:07:14.064
The program is set
for automatic playback

00:07:14.099 --> 00:07:15.191
until it's turned off.

00:07:21.373 --> 00:07:23.500
The baby's missing, too.

00:07:23.542 --> 00:07:24.941
According to the protein decay,

00:07:25.010 --> 00:07:27.410
I'd say Ensign Wildman
replicated this...

00:07:27.446 --> 00:07:29.573
11 hours ago.

00:07:29.614 --> 00:07:30.706
When we get to the Bridge,

00:07:30.749 --> 00:07:32.273
we'll check
the communications logs.

00:07:32.317 --> 00:07:33.648
They might tell us
whether or not...

00:07:40.892 --> 00:07:41.620
There!

00:07:43.662 --> 00:07:45.186
I can't tell if it's humanoid,

00:07:45.230 --> 00:07:47.323
but it's emanating
a bioelectric field.

00:07:47.365 --> 00:07:51.131
Whatever it is, it just
ran into a dead end.

00:08:08.053 --> 00:08:09.680
Over here.

00:08:16.895 --> 00:08:19.693
Something just punched
right through this floor panel

00:08:19.731 --> 00:08:21.323
into the Jefferies tubes.

00:08:21.366 --> 00:08:23.857
What is it?

00:08:23.902 --> 00:08:26.063
Some sort of mucilaginous
compound.

00:08:26.104 --> 00:08:29.562
High concentrations
of amino acids, proteins...

00:08:29.608 --> 00:08:33.135
and fragments
of non-humanoid DNA.

00:08:33.178 --> 00:08:34.668
Well, Ambassador,

00:08:34.713 --> 00:08:39.173
I'd say we've got
an unexpected guest.

00:08:39.217 --> 00:08:42.414
Somehow, I don't think
he's the diplomatic type.

00:08:51.429 --> 00:08:53.294
Main power is failing

00:08:53.331 --> 00:08:56.494
and the environmental controls
are going off-line.

00:08:56.535 --> 00:08:58.969
Systems are starting
to shut down one by one.

00:08:59.070 --> 00:09:00.935
We'd better get to the Bridge.

00:09:15.820 --> 00:09:18.345
Good. We've still
got auxiliary power.

00:09:18.390 --> 00:09:19.618
Deck 1.

00:09:19.658 --> 00:09:21.853
It's getting awfully hot
in here.

00:09:21.893 --> 00:09:23.622
When environmental
controls fail,

00:09:23.662 --> 00:09:25.755
heat from the warp plasma
conduits can't be vented.

00:09:25.797 --> 00:09:27.526
Expect a heat wave before long.

00:09:27.566 --> 00:09:29.534
No problem.
I'm used to it.

00:09:29.568 --> 00:09:31.900
I grew up near
the Rinax marshlands.

00:09:31.937 --> 00:09:34.098
Our summers were the hottest
in the sector...

00:09:34.139 --> 00:09:38.098
50 degrees Celsius,
90 percent humidity.

00:09:38.143 --> 00:09:40.907
And the most vicious lavaflies
you've ever seen.

00:09:40.946 --> 00:09:42.777
Summers in Indiana
were pretty similar

00:09:42.814 --> 00:09:43.906
when I was growing up.

00:09:43.949 --> 00:09:45.712
Except that we had three suns

00:09:45.750 --> 00:09:48.446
and the lavaflies grew
to be six centimeters long.

00:09:48.486 --> 00:09:49.919
Six centimeters, eh?

00:09:49.955 --> 00:09:52.446
Insect repellent was
a booming business.

00:09:56.194 --> 00:09:58.685
There's a life-form
in the turboshaft.

00:09:58.730 --> 00:10:01.790
I'm engaging
the manual override.

00:10:06.538 --> 00:10:08.563
Uh... Captain...

00:10:09.741 --> 00:10:12.403
it sounds like our guest
has brought a few friends.

00:10:12.444 --> 00:10:13.809
One more second.

00:10:13.845 --> 00:10:17.645
I can't get
the pneumatic conduits to...

00:10:22.220 --> 00:10:23.847
That was no lavafly.

00:10:26.424 --> 00:10:28.756
There's no life-form
in the tube above us.

00:10:28.793 --> 00:10:30.784
We're getting out of here.

00:10:43.908 --> 00:10:45.603
Are you all right?

00:10:45.644 --> 00:10:50.411
Yes.
Disgusting, but all right.

00:10:50.448 --> 00:10:52.245
That's the same
mucilaginous compound

00:10:52.284 --> 00:10:54.013
we saw in the transporter room.

00:10:54.052 --> 00:10:55.952
Come on.

00:11:15.774 --> 00:11:16.968
What is it?

00:11:17.008 --> 00:11:19.670
Human life signs.

00:11:19.711 --> 00:11:20.973
Very faint.

00:11:21.012 --> 00:11:22.138
30 or more.

00:11:22.180 --> 00:11:23.738
Where are they coming from?

00:11:23.782 --> 00:11:25.773
Several decks above us.

00:11:25.817 --> 00:11:27.682
I can't pinpoint the location.

00:11:27.719 --> 00:11:29.414
Maybe the crew
is hiding from the aliens

00:11:29.454 --> 00:11:31.183
and they set up
a defense perimeter.

00:11:31.222 --> 00:11:34.123
Maybe.
One thing's for sure...

00:11:34.159 --> 00:11:37.993
whoever's up there,
they're still alive.

00:11:38.096 --> 00:11:39.996
Once we get
the main computer on line,

00:11:40.098 --> 00:11:42.566
we'll be able to get a fix
on their location.

00:12:03.355 --> 00:12:05.050
So hot.

00:12:05.090 --> 00:12:07.217
My head is spinning.

00:12:07.258 --> 00:12:09.556
You've got a high fever,
fluid in your lungs.

00:12:09.594 --> 00:12:10.561
Lung.

00:12:10.595 --> 00:12:11.857
That alien compound
is acting quickly.

00:12:11.896 --> 00:12:12.863
Try to hang on.

00:12:12.897 --> 00:12:14.091
Just three more decks.

00:12:14.132 --> 00:12:15.156
Aye, aye, Captain...

00:12:19.137 --> 00:12:20.126
Captain, go on without me.

00:12:20.171 --> 00:12:21.832
I'm not going
to leave you here, Neelix.

00:12:21.873 --> 00:12:23.670
I can't...

00:12:23.708 --> 00:12:24.868
I'm so dizzy.

00:12:24.909 --> 00:12:26.809
There should be an emergency
medical kit up that tube.

00:12:26.845 --> 00:12:28.904
I'll bring back something
to get you on your feet.

00:12:28.947 --> 00:12:30.175
Don't go away.

00:13:22.966 --> 00:13:25.560
Help! Captain!

00:13:25.602 --> 00:13:27.467
I'm coming, Neelix!

00:13:37.280 --> 00:13:38.907
Neelix!

00:17:53.303 --> 00:17:54.861
This is Captain Kathryn Janeway

00:17:54.904 --> 00:17:56.599
of the Federation
Starship Voyager

00:17:56.639 --> 00:17:57.799
to anyone within range.

00:17:57.841 --> 00:18:00.332
My ship has been seized
by unknown life-forms.

00:18:00.376 --> 00:18:03.004
Require any and all assistance.

00:20:04.701 --> 00:20:06.498
Harry...

00:20:07.503 --> 00:20:08.492
Harry?

00:20:27.390 --> 00:20:28.584
Chakotay.

00:21:38.693 --> 00:21:39.921
Captain.

00:21:39.961 --> 00:21:42.759
Needless to say, I-I thought
you were something else.

00:21:51.072 --> 00:21:53.472
It won't be long before
the other aliens sense you here

00:21:53.508 --> 00:21:54.998
and try to invade Sick Bay.

00:21:55.043 --> 00:21:56.943
We don't have much time
to treat you.

00:21:56.978 --> 00:21:58.946
Doctor, what's going on?

00:21:58.980 --> 00:22:00.174
What are tho?

00:22:03.318 --> 00:22:05.149
You've ruptured
your dorsal extensor muscle

00:22:05.186 --> 00:22:06.778
and bruised two ribs.

00:22:06.821 --> 00:22:08.550
I'm going to have
to perform minor surgery.

00:22:08.590 --> 00:22:11.957
Lie on your side and try
to remain perfectly still.

00:22:11.993 --> 00:22:13.085
Oh...

00:22:13.127 --> 00:22:14.355
Tell me what's happened.

00:22:14.395 --> 00:22:16.955
Voyager has been infected
by a macrovirus.

00:22:17.065 --> 00:22:18.293
A macrovirus?

00:22:18.333 --> 00:22:21.564
A form of life I've never
encountered... or even imagined.

00:22:21.603 --> 00:22:22.865
What about the crew?

00:22:22.904 --> 00:22:24.599
Captain...

00:22:24.639 --> 00:22:26.300
I promise, I will tell you
exactly what happened

00:22:26.341 --> 00:22:28.332
if you just lie still.

00:22:28.376 --> 00:22:31.209
Shortly after you'd left
for the Tak Tak homeworld,

00:22:31.246 --> 00:22:34.374
we received a distress call
from a nearby mining colony...

00:22:34.415 --> 00:22:37.407
a race called the Garans.

00:22:37.452 --> 00:22:38.544
They were experiencing

00:22:38.586 --> 00:22:41.248
what appeared to be
a minor viral outbreak.

00:22:41.289 --> 00:22:42.347
Fever...

00:22:42.390 --> 00:22:44.449
disorientation.

00:22:44.492 --> 00:22:47.427
I think it's some kind
of virus.

00:22:47.462 --> 00:22:51.091
Nothing serious,
but if we don't stop it now,

00:22:51.132 --> 00:22:53.896
we'll be forced
to shut down the operation.

00:22:53.935 --> 00:22:55.766
We may be able to help you.
Doctor?

00:22:55.803 --> 00:22:57.998
A synthetic antigen
may do the trick.

00:22:58.039 --> 00:22:59.802
However, it will
have to be modified

00:22:59.841 --> 00:23:01.001
for the specific virus.

00:23:01.042 --> 00:23:03.169
I'd like to beam down
to the mining colony

00:23:03.211 --> 00:23:05.236
and examine
a few of the infected.

00:23:05.280 --> 00:23:06.372
An away mission.

00:23:06.414 --> 00:23:07.676
I'm the only member
of this crew

00:23:07.715 --> 00:23:08.943
who can successfully enter

00:23:09.017 --> 00:23:11.508
a contaminated environment
without risk.

00:23:11.552 --> 00:23:14.043
Besides, I've been
looking forward

00:23:14.088 --> 00:23:15.953
to spreading my wings.

00:23:16.024 --> 00:23:17.719
Good enough.

00:23:17.759 --> 00:23:20.284
It'll take us about three hours
to reach you.

00:23:20.328 --> 00:23:21.955
Thank you, Commander.

00:23:21.996 --> 00:23:25.557
I don't think we'll...
be going anywhere.

00:23:27.001 --> 00:23:29.526
Prepare to download my program
into the autonomous emitter.

00:23:29.570 --> 00:23:30.628
Yes, Doctor.

00:23:36.644 --> 00:23:38.134
They're not responding
to our hails.

00:23:38.179 --> 00:23:39.271
Life signs.

00:23:39.314 --> 00:23:41.612
There's a lot
of bioelectric interference.

00:23:41.649 --> 00:23:43.241
I can't get a clear reading.

00:23:43.284 --> 00:23:44.649
Perhaps their condition

00:23:44.686 --> 00:23:46.210
is more serious
than they thought.

00:23:46.254 --> 00:23:47.380
I better get down there.

00:23:47.422 --> 00:23:48.446
Doctor, don't forget.

00:23:48.489 --> 00:23:49.478
You're not invulnerable.

00:23:49.524 --> 00:23:51.253
If anything happens
to that portable emitter,

00:23:51.292 --> 00:23:52.418
your program could be lost.

00:23:52.460 --> 00:23:53.484
Don't worry, Commander.

00:23:53.528 --> 00:23:55.758
I've been studying
the Starfleet guidelines

00:23:55.797 --> 00:23:56.957
for away team members.

00:23:56.998 --> 00:23:58.488
For this particular scenario...

00:23:58.533 --> 00:24:00.763
Medical Emergency
on Alien Terrain...

00:24:00.802 --> 00:24:02.269
it is recommended that we keep

00:24:02.303 --> 00:24:03.930
an open com channel
at all times.

00:24:03.971 --> 00:24:04.960
You heard the man.

00:24:06.474 --> 00:24:08.442
Channel open.

00:24:15.817 --> 00:24:17.648
Away team to Voyager.

00:24:17.685 --> 00:24:20.347
Transport was successful,
and my portable emitter

00:24:20.388 --> 00:24:21.912
is working perfectly.

00:24:21.956 --> 00:24:25.824
I am scanning the mine shaft
and proceeding on vector 147.

00:24:25.860 --> 00:24:29.227
Ambient temperature
is 16 degrees Celsius.

00:24:29.263 --> 00:24:31.493
Cavern illumination is minimal,

00:24:31.532 --> 00:24:33.830
but shouldn't pose a problem
for my optical sensors.

00:24:33.868 --> 00:24:36.302
The cave walls
are comprised of granite

00:24:36.337 --> 00:24:37.770
with a mixture of pyroclastic...

00:24:37.805 --> 00:24:40.239
Doctor, I appreciate
your attention to detail,

00:24:40.274 --> 00:24:41.866
but we don't need
that much information.

00:24:41.909 --> 00:24:44.309
Let us know when you've
found the miners.

00:24:44.345 --> 00:24:45.642
Oh. Very well.

00:24:45.680 --> 00:24:47.204
Stand by then.

00:24:51.319 --> 00:24:53.583
Voyager, I've found
one of the miners.

00:25:00.495 --> 00:25:01.928
He appears to be suffering

00:25:01.963 --> 00:25:04.830
from the advanced stages
of severe viral infection.

00:25:04.866 --> 00:25:05.890
Can you treat him?

00:25:05.933 --> 00:25:08.663
Not without a more specialized
immunizing agent.

00:25:12.840 --> 00:25:14.899
This is curious.

00:25:14.942 --> 00:25:16.603
The virus has begun
to concentrate

00:25:16.644 --> 00:25:18.407
in a region near his neck,

00:25:18.446 --> 00:25:19.936
and it's using
his glandular tissue

00:25:19.981 --> 00:25:23.144
to create some sort of...
orifice.

00:25:25.586 --> 00:25:27.213
Something is emerging.

00:25:31.092 --> 00:25:33.117
A life-form.

00:25:33.161 --> 00:25:37.063
Commander, I think
I've just discovered

00:25:37.098 --> 00:25:39.293
a completely new form of life.

00:25:40.735 --> 00:25:42.965
From what I can tell,
it appears to be...

00:25:43.037 --> 00:25:45.403
a macroscopic
version of the virus.

00:25:45.440 --> 00:25:46.805
You mean the virus has grown.

00:25:46.841 --> 00:25:50.641
Yes.
By a factor of billions.

00:25:50.678 --> 00:25:54.205
The virus absorbed
the miner's growth hormones

00:25:54.248 --> 00:25:55.681
into its protein structure

00:25:55.716 --> 00:25:58.685
and used them to increase
its own mass and dimensions.

00:25:58.719 --> 00:26:00.653
In essence,
the virus has found a way

00:26:00.688 --> 00:26:02.315
to leave the microscopic world

00:26:02.356 --> 00:26:04.916
and enter the macroscopic
world... our world.

00:26:06.127 --> 00:26:09.028
It's a remarkable
evolutionary development.

00:26:14.802 --> 00:26:18.363
The virus appears to be
attracted to infrared radiation.

00:26:18.406 --> 00:26:20.567
It's mistaking my holo-matrix
for body heat.

00:26:25.446 --> 00:26:27.778
At the moment,
this one's approximately

00:26:27.815 --> 00:26:31.216
.5 millimeters in diameter,
but it's continuing to grow

00:26:31.252 --> 00:26:33.220
at a rate
of 30 microns every second.

00:26:33.254 --> 00:26:35.415
Commander, permission
to beam the virus aboard

00:26:35.456 --> 00:26:36.445
for further analysis.

00:26:36.491 --> 00:26:37.458
No.

00:26:37.492 --> 00:26:39.153
The virus isn't in our database.

00:26:39.193 --> 00:26:40.956
The biofilters
might not recognize it.

00:26:41.062 --> 00:26:42.825
You'll have to settle
for tricorder data.

00:26:42.864 --> 00:26:44.456
Very well,
but I think I should...

00:26:47.869 --> 00:26:50.667
Stand by, Voyager.

00:26:53.608 --> 00:26:55.371
Hold on. Stop.

00:26:56.377 --> 00:26:59.869
You... you've got to help us.

00:26:59.914 --> 00:27:01.905
I intend to, but first
I must return to my ship

00:27:01.949 --> 00:27:02.916
and prepare an antidote.

00:27:03.017 --> 00:27:04.211
Oh, take me with you.

00:27:04.252 --> 00:27:05.685
I'm afraid that's not possible.

00:27:05.720 --> 00:27:07.085
We'd risk infecting the crew.

00:27:07.121 --> 00:27:09.282
You can't...

00:27:09.323 --> 00:27:11.086
leave me.

00:27:13.160 --> 00:27:15.253
Please.

00:27:16.998 --> 00:27:18.431
Commander Chakotay,

00:27:18.466 --> 00:27:20.730
perhaps if we established
a force field around Sick Bay

00:27:20.768 --> 00:27:22.030
and beamed victims directly...

00:27:22.069 --> 00:27:24.094
I'm sorry, but I'm afraid
we can't take the chance.

00:27:24.138 --> 00:27:25.833
But these people need...

00:27:25.873 --> 00:27:29.104
Doctor, away team guidelines
specifically forbid

00:27:29.143 --> 00:27:31.077
the transport
of unknown infectious...

00:27:31.112 --> 00:27:32.238
Of unknown infectious agents

00:27:32.280 --> 00:27:33.770
onto a starship
without establishing

00:27:33.814 --> 00:27:35.941
containment
and eradication protocols.

00:27:36.050 --> 00:27:38.109
I understand.

00:27:42.156 --> 00:27:44.454
I'll do my best to help you.

00:27:44.492 --> 00:27:46.585
Away team to Voyager.

00:27:46.627 --> 00:27:47.787
One to beam up.

00:27:53.801 --> 00:27:55.291
Doctor to Bridge.

00:27:55.336 --> 00:27:56.803
Checking the biofilters.

00:28:01.342 --> 00:28:03.003
It appears
several viral organisms

00:28:03.044 --> 00:28:04.204
were beamed up as well.

00:28:04.245 --> 00:28:06.213
The biofilter has isolated them.

00:28:06.247 --> 00:28:07.612
Purge the filters.

00:28:07.648 --> 00:28:08.910
Aye, sir.

00:28:09.016 --> 00:28:11.314
Purging is complete.

00:28:11.352 --> 00:28:12.512
I'll be in Sick Bay.

00:28:12.553 --> 00:28:14.851
What I didn't realize

00:28:14.889 --> 00:28:17.551
was that, in the few seconds it
took me to purge the filters,

00:28:17.592 --> 00:28:19.583
some of the virus
had already migrated

00:28:19.627 --> 00:28:21.151
into the transporter buffer.

00:28:21.228 --> 00:28:22.252
Any luck?

00:28:22.296 --> 00:28:24.287
I'm creating a synthetic antigen

00:28:24.332 --> 00:28:26.732
that will inhibit the virus's
ability to replicate,

00:28:26.767 --> 00:28:28.257
but I haven't quite figured out

00:28:28.302 --> 00:28:29.894
how to restore
the infected cells

00:28:29.937 --> 00:28:31.768
to their original condition.

00:28:31.806 --> 00:28:34.036
As for the larger versions
of the viruses...

00:28:34.075 --> 00:28:36.339
what I've termed
the macrovirus...

00:28:36.377 --> 00:28:39.039
I would suggest a flyswatter.

00:28:39.080 --> 00:28:40.775
How long
before the antigen's ready?

00:28:40.815 --> 00:28:43.079
I'd say another 12 hours.

00:28:43.117 --> 00:28:45.415
That gives us time
to rendezvous with the Captain.

00:28:45.453 --> 00:28:47.284
We'll deal with this
after she's aboard.

00:28:47.321 --> 00:28:50.256
Commander, I'd like to apologize

00:28:50.291 --> 00:28:52.592
for my overzealous behavior
on the away mission.

00:28:52.725 --> 00:28:55.660
Compassion is nothing
to be sorry about, Doctor.

00:28:55.695 --> 00:28:57.253
It won't be the last
time you're faced

00:28:57.296 --> 00:28:58.729
with a moral dilemma
in the field.

00:28:58.764 --> 00:29:00.823
But if it makes you
feel any better,

00:29:00.866 --> 00:29:03.630
your performance was...
exemplary.

00:29:03.669 --> 00:29:04.931
Thank you.

00:29:06.706 --> 00:29:08.196
I told you he'd understand.

00:29:08.240 --> 00:29:10.572
Yes. You did.

00:29:12.178 --> 00:29:13.736
We continued working
on the antigen.

00:29:13.779 --> 00:29:17.010
Unfortunately, the macrovirus
was working faster.

00:29:17.049 --> 00:29:19.279
It had already moved
from the transporter buffer

00:29:19.318 --> 00:29:21.513
into an adjacent system.

00:29:29.228 --> 00:29:30.752
B'Elanna, thank God you're here.

00:29:30.796 --> 00:29:32.423
The natives
are getting restless.

00:29:32.465 --> 00:29:33.659
What's the emergency?

00:29:33.699 --> 00:29:34.927
Well, I volunteered

00:29:35.034 --> 00:29:37.468
to help out while Neelix
is away on the trade mission.

00:29:37.503 --> 00:29:39.232
The heating array overloaded.

00:29:39.271 --> 00:29:41.933
It incinerated
a 12-kilo pot roast

00:29:42.008 --> 00:29:44.067
and all the food replicators
went off-line.

00:29:44.110 --> 00:29:45.600
Mmm. Looks delicious.

00:29:45.645 --> 00:29:46.942
Maybe there's a problem

00:29:46.979 --> 00:29:49.743
with the bio-neural gel pack
in the replicator panel.

00:29:51.217 --> 00:29:52.479
Actually...

00:29:52.518 --> 00:29:55.612
I'm a pretty good cook when
Engineering's doing its job.

00:29:57.289 --> 00:29:59.189
Oh, so this is my fault.

00:29:59.225 --> 00:30:01.750
Well, the gel packs are your
department, aren't they?

00:30:01.794 --> 00:30:03.921
Besides, what was
I supposed to tell

00:30:03.963 --> 00:30:06.056
all these hungry,
irritable people?

00:30:06.098 --> 00:30:08.532
You know, I think
that there's a plasma relay

00:30:08.567 --> 00:30:09.966
on Deck 7
that really needs repairs.

00:30:10.036 --> 00:30:12.470
Oh, no, you can't leave
me now, Lieutenant.

00:30:12.505 --> 00:30:13.802
Oh, you need me.

00:30:13.839 --> 00:30:15.466
I'm touched.

00:30:18.678 --> 00:30:20.839
What's going on here?

00:30:20.880 --> 00:30:23.781
It looks like this gel pack
has an infection.

00:30:23.816 --> 00:30:26.080
Half the neurodes
have been burned out

00:30:26.118 --> 00:30:27.380
and the pack is filled

00:30:27.420 --> 00:30:29.718
with some kind
of mucilaginous compound.

00:30:29.755 --> 00:30:32.280
Tom, call the Doctor
and tell him...

00:30:33.325 --> 00:30:34.883
B'Elanna!

00:30:46.005 --> 00:30:48.405
Were any other gel packs
infected?

00:30:48.441 --> 00:30:50.170
No, just the one
in the Mess Hall.

00:30:50.209 --> 00:30:51.608
The ship is healthy.

00:30:51.644 --> 00:30:53.441
It's the crew
we have to worry about.

00:30:53.479 --> 00:30:55.743
Your bones have healed,
but the surrounding tissue

00:30:55.781 --> 00:30:57.715
will be sensitive
for a few days.

00:30:59.418 --> 00:31:01.283
It's getting warmer in here.

00:31:01.320 --> 00:31:03.788
I'm afraid it's not
just the ship, Captain.

00:31:03.823 --> 00:31:04.949
It's also you.

00:31:05.024 --> 00:31:06.821
You've been infected
with the macrovirus.

00:31:06.859 --> 00:31:08.326
You're experiencing
a high fever.

00:31:08.360 --> 00:31:11.193
Yes, on the Bridge, I was
bitten by one of them.

00:31:11.230 --> 00:31:14.199
Your glandular system
is already being affected.

00:31:14.233 --> 00:31:16.098
If I don't treat you now,

00:31:16.135 --> 00:31:17.693
you'll end up like
the rest of the crew.

00:31:19.605 --> 00:31:22.870
I've spent the past few hours
perfecting the antigen...

00:31:22.908 --> 00:31:25.968
but I haven't tested it
on a live subject yet.

00:31:26.011 --> 00:31:28.479
Looks like I'll have to be
your guinea pig, Doctor.

00:31:28.514 --> 00:31:30.744
The crew... why are they
all in the Mess Hall

00:31:30.783 --> 00:31:31.943
and the cargo bays?

00:31:31.984 --> 00:31:33.975
I believe
the larger macroviruses

00:31:34.019 --> 00:31:35.987
are driven
by some sort of instinct

00:31:36.021 --> 00:31:38.182
to assemble
their host population.

00:31:38.224 --> 00:31:41.125
Tell me what happened
after B'Elanna was exposed

00:31:41.160 --> 00:31:42.752
to the infected gel pack.

00:31:44.130 --> 00:31:46.997
I was faced
with an imminent epidemic.

00:31:52.738 --> 00:31:54.865
Oh, no.

00:31:54.907 --> 00:31:57.239
Doctor to the Bridge.

00:31:57.276 --> 00:31:59.244
The macrovirus
is on board Voyager

00:31:59.278 --> 00:32:01.678
and appears to be... airborne.

00:32:01.714 --> 00:32:03.944
I suggest a level-4 quarantine
of the Mess Hall

00:32:03.983 --> 00:32:04.950
and all adjoining sections.

00:32:04.984 --> 00:32:06.679
Acknowledged. Red Alert.

00:32:06.719 --> 00:32:08.949
Initiate level-4 quarantine
protocols on Deck 2.

00:32:08.988 --> 00:32:10.012
Aye, sir.

00:32:11.991 --> 00:32:14.391
All hands,
this is Commander Chakotay.

00:32:14.426 --> 00:32:17.088
We've detected an airborne virus
in the Mess Hall.

00:32:17.129 --> 00:32:18.528
Deck 2 is under quarantine.

00:32:18.564 --> 00:32:21.362
No crew member,
repeat, no crew member

00:32:21.400 --> 00:32:23.925
is to leave or enter
any section on Deck 2.

00:32:23.969 --> 00:32:25.630
Stand by
for further instructions.

00:32:25.671 --> 00:32:27.332
I've erected
the biocontainment fields.

00:32:27.373 --> 00:32:29.841
The area has been sealed.

00:32:29.875 --> 00:32:32.139
We managed to avoid
a ship-wide outbreak,

00:32:32.178 --> 00:32:35.614
but every crew member on Deck 2
had been contaminated.

00:32:35.648 --> 00:32:38.674
I collected a single live
specimen of the macrovirus,

00:32:38.717 --> 00:32:41.709
and returned to Sick Bay
in hopes of finding a cure.

00:32:42.721 --> 00:32:44.211
Ready, Doctor.

00:32:44.256 --> 00:32:46.247
Optimal magnification.

00:32:46.292 --> 00:32:48.419
The specimen has synthesized

00:32:48.460 --> 00:32:50.985
B'Elanna's growth hormone
into its own structure.

00:32:51.030 --> 00:32:52.657
Excellent.
That should give us

00:32:52.698 --> 00:32:54.188
the information we need
to destroy the virus

00:32:54.233 --> 00:32:56.565
without killing its host cells.

00:33:00.039 --> 00:33:03.065
The virus has grown
by 150 microns.

00:33:03.108 --> 00:33:05.406
Its rate of growth
shouldn't hinder our analysis,

00:33:05.444 --> 00:33:07.742
as long as its genetic structure
stays the same.

00:33:13.519 --> 00:33:15.111
Doctor...

00:33:15.154 --> 00:33:17.486
Computer, erect
a level-3 force field

00:33:17.523 --> 00:33:18.683
around the microscope station.

00:33:30.803 --> 00:33:32.998
Well, so much for lunch.

00:33:35.107 --> 00:33:37.473
I may never look at food again.

00:33:37.509 --> 00:33:40.876
I thought Klingons
didn't get nauseated.

00:33:40.913 --> 00:33:43.711
You have a redundant stomach.

00:33:43.749 --> 00:33:46.377
Well, right now...

00:33:46.418 --> 00:33:48.249
they're both unhappy.

00:34:03.636 --> 00:34:05.866
Paris to Sick Bay.

00:34:05.905 --> 00:34:07.099
Go ahead, Lieutenant.

00:34:07.139 --> 00:34:10.267
I just saw two macroviruses
come out of B'Elanna's neck.

00:34:10.309 --> 00:34:11.503
Stand by, Mr. Paris.

00:34:11.543 --> 00:34:13.204
We're close to formulating
an antigen.

00:34:13.245 --> 00:34:16.737
The virus has grown
to.3 meters.

00:34:18.884 --> 00:34:20.078
On the microscopic level,

00:34:20.119 --> 00:34:22.110
the virus uses
that needle-like projection

00:34:22.154 --> 00:34:23.951
to penetrate a cell membrane.

00:34:24.023 --> 00:34:26.048
On our level,
it probably impales

00:34:26.091 --> 00:34:27.718
its victim in much the same way

00:34:27.760 --> 00:34:30.126
infusing him
with its own genetic code.

00:34:31.196 --> 00:34:32.959
The antigen is ready.

00:34:33.032 --> 00:34:34.829
Kes...

00:34:39.004 --> 00:34:41.871
Computer,
deactivate force field.

00:34:50.382 --> 00:34:52.612
Well...

00:34:55.688 --> 00:34:58.782
one down, ten billion to go.

00:35:01.427 --> 00:35:04.089
Eager to inoculate
those already infected,

00:35:04.129 --> 00:35:06.393
I quickly headed
for the quarantined area.

00:35:06.432 --> 00:35:08.093
Though their condition
had grown worse,

00:35:08.133 --> 00:35:10.727
it was the least
of our problems.

00:35:10.769 --> 00:35:12.134
Lieutenant...

00:35:12.171 --> 00:35:14.196
if you can hear me,

00:35:14.239 --> 00:35:17.072
I'm going to give you
an injection.

00:35:17.109 --> 00:35:18.770
It should eliminate the virus.

00:35:18.811 --> 00:35:21.974
What? What is that?

00:35:23.916 --> 00:35:25.713
You don't want to know.

00:35:39.365 --> 00:35:40.332
Doctor to the Bridge.

00:35:40.366 --> 00:35:43.858
Intruder alert.
Deck 2, Section 13.

00:35:43.902 --> 00:35:46.496
Within minutes,
dozens of the larger organisms

00:35:46.538 --> 00:35:49.871
forced their way beyond Deck 2
and overwhelmed the ship.

00:35:49.908 --> 00:35:52.536
It wasn't long before the crew
was incapacitated.

00:35:52.578 --> 00:35:54.978
Although I've developed
an effective vaccine,

00:35:55.080 --> 00:35:56.638
I can't administer it.

00:35:56.682 --> 00:35:58.673
Every time I try to get
to the crew, I'm attacked.

00:35:58.717 --> 00:36:00.742
Perhaps with your help.

00:36:00.786 --> 00:36:03.812
How many of the larger
macroviruses are there?

00:36:03.856 --> 00:36:05.483
I have no way of knowing.

00:36:05.524 --> 00:36:06.923
Dozens, perhaps hundreds.

00:36:06.992 --> 00:36:08.687
They're replicating
at an exponential rate.

00:36:08.727 --> 00:36:11.127
By this time tomorrow,
there could be thousands.

00:36:13.332 --> 00:36:14.731
Speak of the devil.

00:36:22.139 --> 00:36:23.629
You're cured.

00:36:23.674 --> 00:36:24.936
The question is:

00:36:25.009 --> 00:36:27.876
How do we cure
the rest of the crew?

00:36:27.912 --> 00:36:30.312
This antigen...
can it be distributed

00:36:30.347 --> 00:36:31.746
in a gaseous form?

00:36:31.782 --> 00:36:33.647
For absorption via
the respiratory system?

00:36:33.684 --> 00:36:35.276
I've already considered
dispensing it

00:36:35.319 --> 00:36:36.650
through environmental
controls.

00:36:36.687 --> 00:36:37.676
But they're off-line

00:36:37.721 --> 00:36:39.780
and I have limited
engineering expertise.

00:36:39.823 --> 00:36:40.790
Leave that to me.

00:36:40.824 --> 00:36:41.950
All we have to do is get

00:36:42.059 --> 00:36:43.856
to Environmental Control
on Deck 12.

00:36:43.894 --> 00:36:45.486
Easier said than done.

00:36:45.529 --> 00:36:46.894
We'll run into the same problem
I faced

00:36:46.931 --> 00:36:48.330
when I tried to get
to the Mess Hall.

00:36:48.365 --> 00:36:49.662
Not if I can help it.

00:36:49.700 --> 00:36:52.260
Prepare two canisters
of antigen.

00:36:52.303 --> 00:36:54.328
We'll split up
and take different routes

00:36:54.371 --> 00:36:55.702
to Environmental Control.

00:36:55.739 --> 00:36:57.070
It'll double our chances.

00:36:57.107 --> 00:36:59.735
If you get there first, call me

00:36:59.777 --> 00:37:01.267
and I'll talk you
through the repairs.

00:37:01.312 --> 00:37:04.076
The macroviruses are attracted
to infrared radiation.

00:37:04.114 --> 00:37:06.912
Set your tricorder to emit
a thermal scattering signal.

00:37:07.017 --> 00:37:08.780
It will make it more
difficult to target you.

00:37:08.819 --> 00:37:10.582
Ready when you are.

00:37:16.560 --> 00:37:18.619
We'll be right with you.

00:37:28.205 --> 00:37:29.900
Take Jefferies Tube 11.

00:37:31.508 --> 00:37:32.805
What's wrong?

00:37:32.843 --> 00:37:34.834
I've been studying the
ship's infrastructure

00:37:34.878 --> 00:37:36.072
and I'm familiar
with most of it,

00:37:36.113 --> 00:37:38.445
but how do I get there
from here?

00:37:38.482 --> 00:37:39.949
Jefferies Tube 11.

00:37:39.984 --> 00:37:41.747
Take a left at Section 31.

00:37:41.785 --> 00:37:43.480
Head straight down
past the tractor beam emitter

00:37:43.520 --> 00:37:44.509
until you hit Deck 10.

00:37:44.555 --> 00:37:45.522
Get out at Section 3

00:37:45.556 --> 00:37:47.046
and follow the corridor
all the way around...

00:37:47.091 --> 00:37:48.058
Until I hit the shuttle bay.

00:37:48.092 --> 00:37:50.117
Then I crawl through
Access Port 9,

00:37:50.160 --> 00:37:52.458
go past three airlocks
and then two decks down.

00:37:52.496 --> 00:37:54.191
Environmental Control's
at the end of the hall.

00:37:54.231 --> 00:37:55.220
Now I remember.

00:37:56.834 --> 00:37:58.597
Who designed this ship,
anyway?

00:37:58.636 --> 00:37:59.660
Good luck.

00:38:29.199 --> 00:38:30.666
Doctor to Captain Janeway.

00:38:30.701 --> 00:38:32.566
Go ahead.

00:38:32.603 --> 00:38:34.935
I won't be joining you
as soon as I'd hoped.

00:38:34.972 --> 00:38:36.940
The macroviruses overwhelmed me
on Deck 10

00:38:37.041 --> 00:38:39.942
and my portable emitter
was nearly destroyed.

00:38:40.044 --> 00:38:44.071
I've taken refuge inside the
shuttle bay in a shuttlecraft.

00:38:44.114 --> 00:38:45.513
Stay put, Doctor.

00:38:45.549 --> 00:38:48.177
I'm close
to environmental control.

00:39:06.170 --> 00:39:07.797
Janeway to Doctor.

00:39:07.838 --> 00:39:10.068
I've got the environmental
controls back on line.

00:39:10.107 --> 00:39:13.304
Set the dispersal nodes
to one part per thousand.

00:39:16.146 --> 00:39:17.238
What's going on?

00:39:17.281 --> 00:39:18.407
I'm not sure,

00:39:18.449 --> 00:39:20.713
but I think
someone's firing at Voyager.

00:39:20.751 --> 00:39:22.480
Doctor,
use the shuttle's sensors

00:39:22.519 --> 00:39:24.817
to find out what's happening
and patch the data to me.

00:39:24.855 --> 00:39:26.049
Aye, Captain.

00:39:30.394 --> 00:39:33.227
It's the Tak Tak.

00:39:35.065 --> 00:39:37.465
Doctor, open a channel
and hail their Captain.

00:39:37.501 --> 00:39:39.765
Stand by.

00:39:39.803 --> 00:39:41.031
Consul, this is Captain Janeway.

00:39:41.071 --> 00:39:43.369
Why are you firing at us?

00:39:43.407 --> 00:39:45.341
The Garan mining colony,
infected.

00:39:45.375 --> 00:39:46.637
We purified them.

00:39:46.677 --> 00:39:48.144
Your distress call received.

00:39:48.178 --> 00:39:49.372
Voyager infected.

00:39:49.413 --> 00:39:50.937
We are purifying you.

00:39:51.014 --> 00:39:52.538
Purifying?
You're trying to destroy us.

00:39:52.583 --> 00:39:54.175
No choice.

00:39:54.218 --> 00:39:55.685
No cure for the virus.

00:39:55.719 --> 00:39:57.812
Voyager's existence a threat.

00:39:57.855 --> 00:39:59.948
Your illness.
Our apologies.

00:39:59.990 --> 00:40:00.957
Wait.

00:40:00.991 --> 00:40:02.686
We've developed a cure.

00:40:02.726 --> 00:40:04.125
But your torpedoes
just stopped us

00:40:04.161 --> 00:40:06.493
from getting it to our crew
and putting an end to this.

00:40:06.530 --> 00:40:07.963
Cure?

00:40:08.031 --> 00:40:09.498
Yes. A synthetic antigen.

00:40:09.533 --> 00:40:10.625
We've tested it, and it works.

00:40:10.667 --> 00:40:11.861
I can prove it to you.

00:40:11.902 --> 00:40:14.302
And I'd be willing to share
the antigen with your people,

00:40:14.338 --> 00:40:16.602
but first, you've got
to stop attacking my ship.

00:40:16.640 --> 00:40:18.335
Give me a chance
to save my crew.

00:40:18.375 --> 00:40:19.672
A chance.

00:40:19.710 --> 00:40:21.302
One hour.

00:40:27.017 --> 00:40:28.541
Doctor, we've got a problem.

00:40:28.585 --> 00:40:31.213
That last torpedo destroyed
the secondary power couplings.

00:40:31.255 --> 00:40:34.281
I can't get the environmental
controls back on line.

00:40:35.459 --> 00:40:37.984
We appear to be low on options.

00:40:38.028 --> 00:40:40.553
The only systems
we still have access to

00:40:40.597 --> 00:40:42.758
are the ones
with independent power sources...

00:40:42.800 --> 00:40:45.963
shuttlecraft, life-support,
the holodecks...

00:40:48.272 --> 00:40:50.672
Doctor, you said
the macroviruses

00:40:50.707 --> 00:40:52.971
are attracted
to infrared signatures.

00:40:53.010 --> 00:40:54.102
That's right.

00:40:54.144 --> 00:40:57.011
Right now, you and I are
the only targets left on board.

00:40:57.114 --> 00:41:00.948
What if we gave them something
new to sink their teeth into?

00:41:00.984 --> 00:41:02.611
What are you suggesting?

00:41:22.406 --> 00:41:24.397
Doctor, it seems to be working.

00:41:24.441 --> 00:41:26.375
I've programmed
the holo-characters

00:41:26.410 --> 00:41:27.809
to react to the viruses.

00:41:27.845 --> 00:41:29.244
We don't have much time.

00:41:29.279 --> 00:41:31.247
Grab your hypospray
and get to the crew.

00:41:31.281 --> 00:41:32.646
You've got a clear path
to the Mess Hall

00:41:32.683 --> 00:41:34.378
and both cargo bays.

00:41:34.418 --> 00:41:35.442
Acknowledged.

00:41:35.485 --> 00:41:36.816
What about you, Captain?

00:41:36.854 --> 00:41:40.915
I've put together what you
might call an "antigen bomb."

00:41:40.958 --> 00:41:43.483
Now all I have to do
is drop it.

00:43:02.673 --> 00:43:04.504
Doctor to Captain Janeway.

00:43:05.509 --> 00:43:06.908
Captain, please respond.

00:43:08.078 --> 00:43:09.602
Go ahead.

00:43:09.646 --> 00:43:10.670
It worked.

00:43:10.714 --> 00:43:13.444
The macroviruses
have been destroyed.

00:43:13.483 --> 00:43:15.383
And the ship?

00:43:16.653 --> 00:43:19.451
There was heavy damage suffered
on Holodeck 2,

00:43:19.489 --> 00:43:21.320
but there are
no hull breaches in evidence.

00:43:24.761 --> 00:43:25.887
Astonishment.

00:43:25.929 --> 00:43:27.692
Your vessel, purified.

00:43:27.731 --> 00:43:30.393
And we'd be willing to share
the cure with you,

00:43:30.434 --> 00:43:34.302
if you'd be kind enough
to forego destroying our ship.

00:43:34.338 --> 00:43:35.600
Of course, of course.

00:43:35.639 --> 00:43:37.504
Purification will cease.

00:43:37.541 --> 00:43:38.735
My word.

00:43:38.775 --> 00:43:41.744
Many thanks, Captain of Voyager.

00:43:43.013 --> 00:43:44.344
Good health.

00:43:49.419 --> 00:43:50.852
Good health.

00:43:58.862 --> 00:44:00.261
Come in.

00:44:01.965 --> 00:44:03.455
Good morning, Captain.

00:44:03.500 --> 00:44:05.058
Here's an update on repairs.

00:44:08.438 --> 00:44:09.427
How's the crew holding up?

00:44:09.473 --> 00:44:10.497
They're fine,

00:44:10.540 --> 00:44:11.734
although the Doctor tells me

00:44:11.775 --> 00:44:14.209
a few people are still
reporting post-viral queasiness.

00:44:14.244 --> 00:44:15.677
I'm not surprised.

00:44:15.712 --> 00:44:17.942
Inform the crew
that I'm granting

00:44:17.981 --> 00:44:20.245
extended R&amp;R for all personnel

00:44:20.283 --> 00:44:21.910
and work out
the shift rotations.

00:44:21.952 --> 00:44:23.419
Aye, Captain.

00:44:23.453 --> 00:44:25.614
Speaking of R&amp;R...

00:44:25.655 --> 00:44:27.555
a few of us are going skiing
on the holodeck...

00:44:27.591 --> 00:44:28.751
the Ktarian glaciers.

00:44:28.792 --> 00:44:30.521
Fresh air, good workout.

00:44:30.560 --> 00:44:32.187
Care to join us?

00:44:32.229 --> 00:44:33.787
No, thank you, but have fun.

00:44:33.830 --> 00:44:35.354
Not your cup of tea?

00:44:35.399 --> 00:44:36.957
Oh, on the contrary,
I love to ski.

00:44:37.067 --> 00:44:38.728
Let's just say...

00:44:38.769 --> 00:44:41.329
I've had enough of a workout
for the time being.

00:44:42.773 --> 00:44:44.400
Understood.
